    <TD align="left">
    GAAP requires that when a building is purchased certain
    intangible assets (such as above- and below-market leases,
    tenant relationships and in-place lease costs) are allocated
    separately from the building and are amortized over
    significantly shorter lives than the depreciation recognized on
    the building. These intangible assets are not recognized for
